399 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 335 0 R
/E (           Our design journey consisted of mainly refining the look and navigation experience of our solution. After brainstorming many different ideas, we settled on developing a browser extension as it fulfilled our goals of simplicity and accessibility. The initial concept sketches featured multiple steps and prompts to guide users, but once we transitioned to Figma, our ideas became easier to visualize and iterate on. Through that we maintained our goals by moving around steps and keeping early iterations black and white. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2 3]
>>
endobj
400 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 335 0 R
/E (          Progress was largely driven by depending on user testing, demographic research, and analysis of competitors, as well as the market. Below is a breakdown of each prototype stage and what we learned: )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
